{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And a new king arose over Egypt, etc.</b> Even though his memory was preserved in the chronicles of the kings without doubt — particularly regarding the innovation that he enacted as law — the possibility that he might have been from this people, and that this man would have been worthy of showing favor to his people on his account, did not enter the heart of the new king."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Sforno is referring to Joseph: despite the chronicles recording Joseph's decree, the new king did not consider that Joseph was of Israelite origin and thus worthy of gratitude."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:58.032064662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}